menu "Profile: usound (wired USB headset)"

    config USOUND_SPEAKER_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
        int "Speaker sample rate (Hz)"
        default 48000
        range 8000 48000
        help
            What the UAC2 speaker interface advertises and what audio_playback is
            configured for; the two must agree or the feedback servo regulates a
            ring that is filling at a different rate than it drains. 48 kHz is what
            hosts expect of a headset and what Windows selected during the
            2026-09-22 enumeration test.

    config USOUND_SPEAKER_CHANNELS
        int "Speaker channel count"
        default 2
        range 1 2
        help
            FW-AUD-054: 1 or 2. The descriptor's channel cluster and the I2S slot
            configuration both follow this.

    config USOUND_MIC_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
        int "Microphone sample rate (Hz)"
        default 16000
        range 8000 48000
        help
            Independent of the speaker rate: each direction has its own clock source
            entity (FW-AUD-053), which is the point of the duplex descriptor. The
            host read 16 kHz capture beside 48 kHz render on 2026-09-22.

    config USOUND_PLAYBACK_RING_MS
        int "Playback ring capacity (ms of audio)"
        default 60
        range 20 500
        help
            The elastic buffer between the USB host and the I2S clock (ADR-014). It
            must exceed CONFIG_USB_AUDIO_SPEAKER_TARGET_MS plus one packet or
            usb_audio_init() refuses the configuration (FW-AUD-059); the margin above
            that is how much host jitter the ring absorbs before the servo has to
            act. 60 ms at 48 kHz stereo 16-bit is 11520 bytes of internal RAM.

    # Speaker and microphone pins are board wiring shared by every profile:
    # see "Speaker (I2S TX) pins" / "Microphone (I2S RX) pins" in main/Kconfig.projbuild.

endmenu
